1868", "id": "2033290217193361868", "text": "Next cleanliness tool:  SCRAP.  It's for unit test files.  Completely different algorithm.  Maybe.", "raw_text": {"text": "Next cleanliness tool:  SCRAP.  It's for unit test files.  Completely different algorithm.  Maybe.", "display_text_range": [0, 98], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282564, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 3, "reposts": 1, "likes": 17, "bookmarks": 8, "quotes": 0, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Sun Mar 15 21:12:19 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1773609139, "views": 7808, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "source": "Twitter Web App", "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2033282055300059539", "id": "2033282055300059539", "text": "get a load of the DBC and Unit Tests in the ledger example of http://github.com/unclebob/AIR-J", "raw_text": {"text": "get a load of the DBC and Unit Tests in the ledger example of https://t.co/0Qc8S0lqWi", "display_text_range": [0, 85], "facets": [{"type": "url", "indices": [62, 85], "original": "https://t.co/0Qc8S0lqWi", "replacement": "http://github.com/unclebob/AIR-J", "display": "github.com/unclebob/AIR-J"}]}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282564, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 4, "reposts": 4, "likes": 30, "bookmarks": 15, "quotes": 0, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Sun Mar 15 20:39:53 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1773607193, "possibly_sensitive": false, "views": 6354, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "source": "Twitter Web App", "card": {"url": "http://github.com/unclebob/AIR-J", "title": "GitHub - unclebob/AIR-J: A simple language for AIs to use and humans to ignore. This version is JVM...", "description": "A simple language for AIs to use and humans to ignore. This version is JVM based. - unclebob/AIR-J", "domain": "github.com", "image": {"width": 800, "height": 419, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/card_img/2103919723293409280/RsTnGE7V?format=jpg&name=800x419"}}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2033254026096107600", "id": "2033254026096107600", "text": "One of the greatest advantages to an AI is that it helps you to THINK.  It is great at organizing and analyzing and interrogating, and giving just the right information for you to make an informed decision.  \n\nIt's, frankly, breathtaking.", "raw_text": {"text": "One of the greatest advantages to an AI is that it helps you to THINK.  It is great at organizing and analyzing and interrogating, and giving just the right information for you to make an informed decision.  \n\nIt's, frankly, breathtaking.", "display_text_range": [0, 238], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282564, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 72, "reposts": 51, "likes": 646, "bookmarks": 78, "quotes": 7, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Sun Mar 15 18:48:30 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1773600510, "views": 20600, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "source": "Twitter Web App", "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2033246552651649097", "id": "2033246552651649097", "text": "The AI is _very_ focussed on the last thing you told it to do -- the thing it's working on now.  The second to last thing you told it is hard for it to keep in mind.  The third to last is even harder.  Don't depend on those rules you told it at the start.  Don't expect it to always follow what you put in CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md.  The higher those are in it's context window, the less likely they are to be considered.", "raw_text": {"text": "The AI is _very_ focussed on the last thing you told it to do -- the thing it's working on now.  The second to last thing you told it is hard for it to keep in mind.  The third to last is even harder.  Don't depend on those rules you told it at the start.  Don't expect it to always follow what you put in CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md.  The higher those are in it's context window, the less likely they are to be considered.", "display_text_range": [0, 418], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282564, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 22, "reposts": 13, "likes": 153, "bookmarks": 35, "quotes": 0, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Sun Mar 15 18:18:48 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1773598728, "views": 13978, "is_note_tweet": true, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "source": "Twitter Web App", "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2033225747217662138", "id": "2033225747217662138", "text": "I've been crapping and mutating the code like crazy.  It really keeps the code locked down, clean and tidy.  But it doesn't help the tests.\n\nAfter awhile I started getting concerned about the state of the tests, so I asked Codex about that.  It told me the tests needed some serious restructuring.  They were pretty much a hodge-podge of uncorrelated assertions.\n\nI asked Codex whether crap and mutate were good tools to apply to the tests.  It told me that they wouldn't be helpful since tests are a very different kind of code than production code.  (I agree with this BTW).  \n\nSo now I have Codex roaring through the tests and re-partioning  them into a more cogent form.  \n\nNow I'm wondering if there aren't some tools like crap and mutate but that are more geared to tests.  Hmmm.", "raw_text": {"text": "I've been crapping and mutating the code like crazy.  It really keeps the code locked down, clean and tidy.  But it doesn't help the tests.\n\nAfter awhile I started getting concerned about the state of the tests, so I asked Codex about that.  It told me the tests needed some serious restructuring.  They were pretty much a hodge-podge of uncorrelated assertions.\n\nI asked Codex whether crap and mutate were good tools to apply to the tests.  It told me that they wouldn't be helpful since tests are a very different kind of code than production code.  (I agree with this BTW).  \n\nSo now I have Codex roaring through the tests and re-partioning  them into a more cogent form.  \n\nNow I'm wondering if there aren't some tools like crap and mutate but that are more geared to tests.  Hmmm.", "display_text_range": [0, 785], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282564, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http:/